-- חוק הודעה מוקדמת לפיטורים ולהתפטרות, התשס"א-2001 — sections 1, 2, 3, 4,
-- 5, 6, 7, 10, 11 and 12: who is an employee on a salary and who on a wage,
-- and what the regular wage is (by the Severance Pay Law); that an employer
-- who would dismiss, and an employee who would resign, give notice in
-- writing, naming the day it is given and the day the dismissal or the
-- resignation takes effect; the notice an employee on a salary is owed, by
-- the months he has worked, and one on a wage; that the same counts hold for
-- a resignation; that the employer may waive the work in the notice period
-- and pay its regular wage instead; what is owed where no notice is given;
-- where the law asks no notice; that the State is an employer like any
-- other; and that the law takes away no better right. The text is
-- laws/advance-notice-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים
-- הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: no document of the corpus cites the law, but the takanon,
-- the Oz LaTmura agreement and their procedures set when a teacher is
-- dismissed, how long before he hears of it, and how long before he must
-- say he is leaving. When a dismissal the takanon dates takes effect, who of
-- the teachers is on a salary, and whether a longer resignation notice an
-- instrument asks of the teacher is below the floor, is convention
-- instruments.notice-law-teaching, a pick for the lawyer.
--
-- Notice is counted in days. "חודש ימים" is a calendar month, 28 to 31 days;
-- where an instrument is weighed against it, it is counted at its longest,
-- 31 days, so that an instrument found to meet it meets it in every month.
-- A month of work is a completed month.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties

§ `חוק הודעה מוקדמת לפיטורים ולהתפטרות — ההודעה המוקדמת ואורכה`

§§ `1`

-- "The Severance Pay Law": the Severance Pay Law, 1963. "An employee on a
-- salary" and "an employee on a wage": as §12 of that law defines them —
-- one whose pay is set by the month or a longer period, and every other.
-- "The regular wage": the wage counted for severance pay under its §13.
@desc How the Advance Notice Law counts an employee, by section 12 of the Severance Pay Law.
DECLARE `how the Advance Notice Law counts the employee` IS ONE OF
    `an employee on a salary, as the Advance Notice Law counts him`
    `an employee on a wage, as the Advance Notice Law counts him`

@ref law:1
GIVEN `paid by the month or by a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `how the Advance Notice Law counts the employee`
DECIDE `the employee under section 1 of the Advance Notice Law` `paid by the month or by a longer period` IS
    IF `paid by the month or by a longer period`
    THEN `an employee on a salary, as the Advance Notice Law counts him`
    ELSE `an employee on a wage, as the Advance Notice Law counts him`

§§ `2`

-- (א): an employer who would dismiss an employee gives him notice of the
-- dismissal; (ב): an employee who would resign gives his employer notice of
-- the resignation; (ג): in writing, naming the day the notice is given and
-- the day the dismissal or the resignation takes effect. (The employee is,
-- in this corpus, a teaching employee.)
@desc What the Advance Notice Law asks of an employer and of an employee.
DECLARE `Advance Notice Law act` IS ONE OF
    `give the employee written notice of the dismissal, its day and the day it takes effect`
    `give the employer written notice of the resignation, its day and the day it takes effect`

@ref law:2
GIVEN `days of notice owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Advance Notice Law act`
DECIDE `notice of a dismissal under section 2 of the Advance Notice Law` `days of notice owed` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `give the employee written notice of the dismissal, its day and the day it takes effect`
    WITHIN `days of notice owed`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "Advance Notice Law, section 2(א): an employer who would dismiss an employee gives him written notice of the dismissal"

@ref law:2
GIVEN `days of notice owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Advance Notice Law act`
DECIDE `notice of a resignation under section 2 of the Advance Notice Law` `days of notice owed` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `give the employer written notice of the resignation, its day and the day it takes effect`
    WITHIN `days of notice owed`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "Advance Notice Law, section 2(ב): an employee who would resign gives his employer written notice of the resignation"

-- (ג): the notice names the day it is given and the day the dismissal or
-- the resignation takes effect; the days between them are its length.
@ref law:2
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A NUMBER
      `the day it takes effect` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of notice a written notice gives under section 2(ג)` `the day the notice is given` `the day it takes effect` IS
    max 0 (`the day it takes effect` MINUS `the day the notice is given`)

§§ `3`

-- An employee on a salary is owed notice of a dismissal: (1) in his first
-- six months of work, a day for each month of work; (2) from the seventh
-- month to the end of his first year, 6 days and two and a half days more
-- for each month of work in that period; (3) after his first year, a month.
@ref law:3
`a month of notice, counted at its longest` MEANS 31

@ref law:3
GIVEN `months of work completed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of notice section 3 gives an employee on a salary` `months of work completed` IS
    IF `months of work completed` AT MOST 6
    THEN `months of work completed`
    ELSE IF `months of work completed` LESS THAN 12
         THEN 6 PLUS 2.5 TIMES (`months of work completed` MINUS 6)
         ELSE `a month of notice, counted at its longest`

#ASSERT `days of notice section 3 gives an employee on a salary` 2 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `days of notice section 3 gives an employee on a salary` 7 EQUALS 8.5
#ASSERT `days of notice section 3 gives an employee on a salary` 10 EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `days of notice section 3 gives an employee on a salary` 11 EQUALS 18.5
#ASSERT `days of notice section 3 gives an employee on a salary` 13 EQUALS 31

§§ `4`

-- An employee on a wage is owed notice of a dismissal: (1) in his first
-- year, a day for each month of work; (2) in his second year, 14 days and a
-- day more for each two months of work in that year; (3) in his third year,
-- 21 days and a day more for each two months of work in that year; (4)
-- after his third year, a month.
@ref law:4
GIVEN `months of work completed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of notice section 4 gives an employee on a wage` `months of work completed` IS
    IF `months of work completed` LESS THAN 12
    THEN `months of work completed`
    ELSE IF `months of work completed` LESS THAN 24
         THEN 14 PLUS TRUNC ((`months of work completed` MINUS 12) DIVIDED BY 2) 0
         ELSE IF `months of work completed` LESS THAN 36
              THEN 21 PLUS TRUNC ((`months of work completed` MINUS 24) DIVIDED BY 2) 0
              ELSE `a month of notice, counted at its longest`

#ASSERT `days of notice section 4 gives an employee on a wage` 2 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `days of notice section 4 gives an employee on a wage` 11 EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `days of notice section 4 gives an employee on a wage` 15 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `days of notice section 4 gives an employee on a wage` 30 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `days of notice section 4 gives an employee on a wage` 40 EQUALS 31

-- The notice of a dismissal, by how §1 counts the employee.
@ref law:3 law:4
GIVEN e IS A `how the Advance Notice Law counts the employee`
      `months of work completed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of notice the Advance Notice Law asks for a dismissal` e `months of work completed` IS
    IF e EQUALS `an employee on a salary, as the Advance Notice Law counts him`
    THEN `days of notice section 3 gives an employee on a salary` `months of work completed`
    ELSE `days of notice section 4 gives an employee on a wage` `months of work completed`

§§ `5`

-- §§3 and 4 hold, with the changes the matter requires, for notice of a
-- resignation.
@ref law:5
GIVEN e IS A `how the Advance Notice Law counts the employee`
      `months of work completed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of notice the Advance Notice Law asks for a resignation` e `months of work completed` IS
    `days of notice the Advance Notice Law asks for a dismissal` e `months of work completed`

§§ `6`

-- (א): an employer may tell the employee, in the notice of dismissal, that
-- he waives his presence and his work in the notice period, in whole or in
-- part, so long as he pays him the regular wage for the period waived; (ב):
-- so too where the employee gave notice of resignation.
@ref law:6
GIVEN `days of the notice period waived` IS A NUMBER
      `the regular wage for a day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what section 6 of the Advance Notice Law asks for the period waived` `days of the notice period waived` `the regular wage for a day` IS
    `days of the notice period waived` TIMES `the regular wage for a day`

§§ `7`

-- (א): an employer who dismissed an employee without the notice the law
-- asks pays him the regular wage for the period no notice was given for;
-- (ב): an employee who stopped work without notice of resignation pays his
-- employer the same.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `days of notice owed` IS A NUMBER
      `days of notice given` IS A NUMBER
      `the regular wage for a day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what section 7 of the Advance Notice Law asks for notice not given` `days of notice owed` `days of notice given` `the regular wage for a day` IS
    max 0 (`days of notice owed` MINUS `days of notice given`) TIMES `the regular wage for a day`

#ASSERT `what section 7 of the Advance Notice Law asks for notice not given` 31 0 100 EQUALS 3100
#ASSERT `what section 7 of the Advance Notice Law asks for notice not given` 31 40 100 EQUALS 0

§§ `10`

-- §§2 to 7 do not hold (1) for an employee, in special circumstances in
-- which he cannot be asked to work the notice period (the Minister may set
-- them); (2) for an employer, where the employee dismissed is not entitled
-- to severance pay under §16 or §17 of the Severance Pay Law, or under the
-- decision of a disciplinary tribunal that ordered dismissal without it.
-- Whether the circumstances are such is an input: the Severance Pay Law's
-- §16 leaves them to the collective agreement, and its §17, not pinned, to
-- the labour court.
@ref law:10
GIVEN `the employee is not entitled to severance under section 16 or 17 of the Severance Pay Law, or by a disciplinary tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Advance Notice Law asks notice of the dismissal` `the employee is not entitled to severance under section 16 or 17 of the Severance Pay Law, or by a disciplinary tribunal` IF
    NOT `the employee is not entitled to severance under section 16 or 17 of the Severance Pay Law, or by a disciplinary tribunal`

@ref law:10
GIVEN `special circumstances in which the employee cannot be asked to work the notice period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Advance Notice Law asks notice of the resignation` `special circumstances in which the employee cannot be asked to work the notice period` IF
    NOT `special circumstances in which the employee cannot be asked to work the notice period`

§§ `11`

-- For this law, the State is an employer like any other.
@ref law:11
`section 11 makes the State an employer like any other under the Advance Notice Law` MEANS TRUE

§§ `12`

-- The law takes away no right an employee has under a law, a collective
-- agreement or a contract of employment: for a notice measured in days,
-- the longer stands.
@ref law:12
GIVEN `what the law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what the agreement or contract gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what stands under section 12 of the Advance Notice Law` `what the law gives` `what the agreement or contract gives` IS
    max `what the law gives` `what the agreement or contract gives`

#ASSERT `what stands under section 12 of the Advance Notice Law` 16 14 EQUALS 16
